{"id": "EUVD-2026-86786", "enisaUuid": "74fd22d3-efa6-3cd0-b67f-eb44abf01531", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Don't dereference trace_event_file in deferred trigger free\n\nThe enable_event trigger defers trace_event_put_ref() to the\ntrigger free kthread, but the trace_event_file can already be freed\nwhen the instance is removed.\n\nKeep the trace_event_call directly in enable_trigger_data so the\ndeferred free does not access the freed trace_event_file.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/67fb91a7f7bb1d958cf9cc249c912bca9b2fc821", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bcfe2816e6ec46c3f4c58aa4264476665ddb3f69"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97932", "GHSA-pm4h-64gj-cjhp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1d5301c7-3bac-3326-8769-8ed0aa52f5fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.2"}, {"id": "311d513c-2a7c-3cb8-83e9-ec1fd81d81f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "159fdc3e01dca5fdbc412fcd8b239895733a270d"}, {"id": "7d02f04d-5a94-30b3-9ac9-ccd0d342f891", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "a5c0e815-38d0-3478-87db-4c5612c16d76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1.6 <7.2"}, {"id": "a7763b74-c7e5-3f45-b8bd-af8c43aa8bfd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e091351b38818ef620d27f44f4bfd625f13afbff <bcfe2816e6ec46c3f4c58aa4264476665ddb3f69"}, {"id": "c6513f06-f043-389a-917f-ef551201eb1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e346ec2e-299e-3122-8e7e-a6b774397e2d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e091351b38818ef620d27f44f4bfd625f13afbf